      "text": "The deep sea (below 200 m) constitutes ~95% of the ocean's inhabitable volume.\nIt is permanently dark, cold, and under crushing pressure. Yet it is far from lifeless:\nan estimated 10 billion tonnes of biomass exists in the deep ocean, and an extraordinary\nrange of adaptations allows organisms to thrive where nothing \"should\" survive."
    },
