      "text": "ADAPTATION:\n  Trimethylamine N-oxide (TMAO):\n  (CH₃)₃N→O — organic osmolyte\n  Preferentially excluded from protein surface → \"pushes\" water\n  to stabilize protein folding under pressure\n  Concentration: ~40 mmol/kg per 1000 m depth\n  → Mariana snailfish (~8000 m): ~250 mmol/kg TMAO\n  → TMAO may limit maximum fish depth at ~8200 m\n    (beyond this, TMAO concentration would be physiologically\n     incompatible with other metabolic processes)\n```"
